WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.240
While members of superhero teams like&nbsp;
the Avengers and the Justice League&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.120
may save the world in spite of their flaws, when&nbsp;
it comes to the members of the Suicide Squad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.800
without their weaknesses, they wouldn't&nbsp;
even be part of the crew in the first place.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.360
The biggest weakness of Weasel, played&nbsp;
in The Suicide Squad by Sean Gunn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:22.640
is his insatiable bloodthirst. In the source&nbsp;
material, the savage little beast man is part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.920
of one of the most disastrous Task Force X&nbsp;
missions on record in terms of body count,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.520
and Weasel is one of the main&nbsp;
reasons almost no one comes home.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:36.000
In 1988's The Doom Patrol&nbsp;
and Suicide Squad Special #1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.760
Weasel is part of a Squad lineup sent to free&nbsp;
the superhero Hawk from a fortress in Nicaragua.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.800
Rick Flag leads the Squad — which, along&nbsp;
with Weasel, includes Psi, Thinker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.960
and Mr. 104 — and he's also the only survivor.&nbsp;
Psi and Mr. 104 are both killed by the armored&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.600
Soviet soldiers of the Rocket Red Brigade,&nbsp;
while Weasel and Thinker kill each other.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.760
When the Squad runs into members of Doom&nbsp;
Patrol — who are also there hoping to free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:07.840
Hawk — things quickly get tense. Mr. 104, an&nbsp;
old enemy of Doom Patrol, attacks the heroes.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:13.520
When Thinker tries to stop Mr. 104, Weasel&nbsp;
— not caring about 104's grudges but just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:17.840
wanting to spill more blood – rips&nbsp;
Thinker's throat open, killing him.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:22.160
Rick Flag takes Thinker's helmet from&nbsp;
the villain's corpse and uses its power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.880
but unbeknownst to Flag, the villain imprinted the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.320
helmet with the final command to&nbsp;
get revenge on Thinker's killer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.600
Before Flag removes the helmet, it unleashes&nbsp;
a powerful blast, killing Weasel instantly.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:38.800
As to the biggest weakness of John Cena's&nbsp;
Peacemaker, well, it's kind of in the name.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.480
"Be like a douchey Captain America."

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.120
In spite of being on a team with the likes&nbsp;
of Harley Quinn, the gun-toting vigilante&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:52.240
suffers arguably the most singular mental&nbsp;
illness of any other member of Suicide Squad.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.000
Traumatized by the suicide of his&nbsp;
father — a Nazi concentration camp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.680
commander — Peacemaker has developed&nbsp;
the troubling philosophy that peace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.920
is worth any cost, including killing&nbsp;
anyone he deecms an enemy of peace.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.960
"The guy who believes in peace at any cost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.480
no matter how many people he&nbsp;
needs to kill along the way."

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:15.520
His illness goes so far as to make Peacemaker&nbsp;
believe the ghost of his father and the ghosts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:20.720
of the long list of people he's killed speak&nbsp;
to him from inside his strange metal helmet.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:26.080
Peacemaker's internal struggles are enough to make&nbsp;
you wonder why Amanda Waller or anyone else would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.800
ever be willing to recruit him. He may be good&nbsp;
in a fight, but his mental illness is a glaring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:36.080
liability. If an enemy knows what makes Peacemaker&nbsp;
tick and that he hears disembodied voices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.800
he attributes to the dead, it won't take&nbsp;
much to manipulate the vigilante. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.200
if you believe the best road to peace is to&nbsp;
mow down everyone who disagrees with you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.732
imagine what other kinds of insanity&nbsp;
you could be made to believe?

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:54.320
Savant is a genius — and he knows it. While he&nbsp;
doesn't boast any kind of metahuman abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:58.320
his intellect and hand-to-hand fighting&nbsp;
skills make him a formidable opponent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.600
and he isn't shy about letting&nbsp;
you know how dangerous he can be.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.280
Savant originally came on the scene&nbsp;
wanting to become the next Batman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.960
though he would eventually decide to&nbsp;
turn his efforts toward blackmail.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:14.240
In the comics, Savant's time with the Suicide&nbsp;
Squad makes it clear his biggest vulnerability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:19.760
is his arrogance. For example, Savant is a part&nbsp;
of the Squad lineup sent after Harley Quinn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.600
when she goes rogue. After the team&nbsp;
tracks Harley to a police station,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:28.880
Savant constantly butts heads with Deadshot&nbsp;
- almost coming to blows. When Deadshot urges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:35.200
Savant to take Harley seriously as a threat,&nbsp;
saying "Savant, she's dangerous," Savant answers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:39.600
"I'm dangerous. She's just some psycho&nbsp;
looking for her dead boyfriend's face."

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:44.320
Once Savant goes one on one with Harley,&nbsp;
that arrogance nearly leads to his death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:49.200
Harley tricks Savant into charging into a&nbsp;
jail cell where she's hidden a pressure mine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:54.240
Savant is forced to stay there, standing on the&nbsp;
mine, to prevent the explosive from going off.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:58.320
Harley locks him in the cell, and Deadshot&nbsp;
is forced to deal with Harley on his own.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:02.960
King Shark is one of the most physically&nbsp;
powerful members of the Suicide Squad. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:08.160
can breathe underwater and swim as well as any&nbsp;
fish. He's a powerhouse with superhuman strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.640
and he has absolutely no compunction about&nbsp;
not only killing, but eating anyone who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:17.520
gets in his way. Unfortunately, as you might&nbsp;
guess, King Shark isn't the greatest thinker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:22.000
of DC's characters and that can lead to&nbsp;
complications, for him as well as the Squad.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:27.251
"Nanaue, play nice with your brother!"

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.480
True to his name, King Shark is usually thinking&nbsp;
with his stomach if he's thinking at all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:42.000
In 2011's Suicide Squad #2, for example,&nbsp;
as the team battles a stadium full of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.040
grotesquely mutated humans, Deadshot has to&nbsp;
urge King Shark to keep moving because the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:52.080
man-monster keeps stopping to eat his victims.&nbsp;
In the following issue, after Deadshot assures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.960
his teammates that King Shark "knows to keep&nbsp;
a low profile," the action cuts to the aquatic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.760
villain tearing through a farmer's chicken&nbsp;
coop and devouring the poor birds inside.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:06.640
In the volume of Suicide Squad launched&nbsp;
in 2019, it's partly King Shark's lack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:10.800
of intelligence that leads him to become&nbsp;
one of the earliest victims of the comic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:15.520
In the third issue of that series, King Shark&nbsp;
lets his guard down in the presence of his enemy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:20.160
Fin — an aquatic character whose brother&nbsp;
he killed and ate two issues earlier.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:26.000
King Shark's thoughtlessness in the face of danger&nbsp;
comes back to bite him, literally. Fin rewards the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.800
stupidity with poetic justice, summoning&nbsp;
a nearby school of sharks to devour him.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:35.920
Alice Braga's Solsoria doesn't appear&nbsp;
in the Suicide Squad comics or any of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:40.720
DC's publications, so it's tough to nail&nbsp;
down any weaknesses or strengths. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:46.080
one popular theory suggests Solsoria&nbsp;
is a gender-bent version of Juan Soria.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:50.560
If that's the case, then it doesn't bode well&nbsp;
for the future of this mystery character.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:56.960
Juan Soria appears in Suicide Squad #33 and&nbsp;
#34. He's just a regular guy who dreams of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.880
joining the Justice League, and when his&nbsp;
hand is injured in a workplace accident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:07.040
he uses the opportunity to inject nanites into his&nbsp;
body that give him the ability to open any lock.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:12.160
He tries and fails to join the Justice League,&nbsp;
and shortly afterward turns to a life of crime.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:16.720
After the inevitable arrest, Amanda&nbsp;
Waller recruits him into Task Force X,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:21.840
though his metahuman ability has less to do with&nbsp;
her choice than his crippling low self-esteem.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:26.080
She sends the Squad against a powerful&nbsp;
alien who ends up capturing Soria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:30.560
and feeding off his energy. Amusingly,&nbsp;
Soria's self-critical negative feelings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:34.640
cause the alien to shrink to the point&nbsp;
where he can kill it by stepping on it.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:37.920
Juan Soria correctly assumes he's destined to die.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:42.640
He becomes similar to Sam Rockwell's character&nbsp;
Guy Fleegman in the film Galaxy Quest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:46.800
assuming that because he's the new character&nbsp;
with no codename, he'll be the one to die.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:52.000
"My character isn't important enough for a last&nbsp;
name, because I'm gonna die five minutes in."&nbsp;

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.034
"Guy, you have a last name."

00:06:55.034 --> 00:06:56.400
"Do I?!"

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.360
In spite of surviving the battle&nbsp;
against the alien invader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:03.680
he's rewarded for his service by having&nbsp;
his nanite-enhanced hands removed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:08.480
after which it's revealed that he was Waller's&nbsp;
pawn in the plan the whole time. And then Waller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:14.160
puts him in the same cell as Killer Croc, who —&nbsp;
it's strongly implied — uses Soria as a snack.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:18.640
Peter Capaldi's the Thinker is one&nbsp;
of the oldest characters appearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:22.960
in The Suicide Squad. His criminal career&nbsp;
dates back to the Golden Age of comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:27.280
and among other exploits he's one of the&nbsp;
founding members of the Injustice Society.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:32.000
In the comics, the Thinker's abilities stem&nbsp;
from the so-called "Thinking Cap" he wears.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:35.760
The cap gives Thinker access to&nbsp;
powerful psychic abilities such as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:41.280
telepathy and telekinesis. Without the cap,&nbsp;
however, Thinker has no powers to speak of.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:45.920
Even with the cap, physically the Thinker&nbsp;
isn't particularly formidable and he appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:50.320
to be the oldest member of Task Force X.&nbsp;
This is similar to Thinker's situation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:56.560
in the comics. When he joins Task Force X in&nbsp;
1988's Doom Patrol and Suicide Squad Special,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:00.240
he warns his teammates that he plans&nbsp;
to succeed in his mission and stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:04.720
anyone who gets in his way because he's&nbsp;
"growing old" and the pardon he's meant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:08.800
to receive for his service is necessary&nbsp;
to live the rest of his life in peace.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.200
But the Thinker doesn't survive long&nbsp;
enough to retire. When things go sideways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:17.920
his teammate Weasel kills him with a single&nbsp;
swipe of his claw. Thinker's biggest weakness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:22.960
then, is his physical vulnerability. His psychic&nbsp;
powers make it difficult to get to him, but if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:27.440
somehow you manage to reach him as Weasel does,&nbsp;
then it doesn't take much to incapacitate him.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:33.280
As the head of Task Force X, Amanda Waller&nbsp;
(a.k.a. "The Wall") spends most of her time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:37.760
behind the scenes, monitoring the team and&nbsp;
making sure they do what they're supposed to do.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:42.240
When the explosives in one of the recruits'&nbsp;
necks goes off, there's a pretty good chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:46.880
it's Waller giving the order to detonate.&nbsp;
Waller is just as ruthless as the worst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:52.720
villains she brings into Task Force X, and can be&nbsp;
just as cold-blooded. She has absolutely no moral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:57.760
qualms about feeding any of her recruits into the&nbsp;
meat grinder, including ordering their deaths.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:01.680
The challenge Waller tends to face in&nbsp;
every incarnation of the Suicide Squad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.520
is that while she may be the top&nbsp;
dog when it comes to Task Force X,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:10.400
she's part of a government bureaucracy that will&nbsp;
only allow her to go so far outside the box.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:15.840
The original Suicide Squad run, for example,&nbsp;
includes storylines in which rival politicians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:20.240
target Waller, using their knowledge of&nbsp;
the Suicide Squad's actions as leverage.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:24.960
As much as she may want it to be, Waller's&nbsp;
rule over the Suicide Squad is not absolute.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:30.160
She's reminded of this in 2019's Suicide&nbsp;
Squad #1, when the new volume opens with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:35.040
the control of Task Force X being taken&nbsp;
from her by the even more coldhearted Lok.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:39.840
In The Suicide Squad, Flula Borg&nbsp;
will play the former Olympic athlete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:44.960
Javelin. The crook carries a high-tech cache&nbsp;
of explosive spears and he's been both a member&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:50.880
of and enemy to the Suicide Squad a number of&nbsp;
times in the comics, including the 2005 volume&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:56.400
of Deadshot in which Javelin joins a team of&nbsp;
villains wanting revenge on the expert marksman.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:00.800
Javelin's biggest weakness is fairly&nbsp;
obvious: With no metahuman abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:05.440
he's highly dependent on his gimmick weaponry.&nbsp;
As an athlete in peak physical condition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.560
his hand-to-hand combat skills&nbsp;
are nothing to sneeze at,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:12.880
but without the weapons that make up&nbsp;
his namesake, Javelin won't last long.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:16.720
Not to mention that even when he does have&nbsp;
his spears, they're not always a help.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:21.440
Like just about any comic book supervillain who's&nbsp;
been around long enough, Javelin has been killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:26.480
a number of times only to be resurrected, and&nbsp;
more often that not it's been in part his own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:32.400
spears that kill him. In Deadshot #5, for example,&nbsp;
the marksman kills Javelin by shooting one of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:38.480
explosive spears while it's still in his hand.&nbsp;
Years earlier in 1991's War of the Gods #3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:42.832
the sorceress Circe kills Javelin&nbsp;
by impaling him on his own spear.

00:10:43.448 --> 00:10:47.840
There have been at least three different comic&nbsp;
book versions of Bloodsport, though in The Suicide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:52.880
Squad Idris Elba is set to play the original&nbsp;
— Robert DuBois, who comes close to killing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:59.040
Superman in 1987's Superman #4 after shooting&nbsp;
the Man of Steel with a sliver of kryptonite.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:04.480
If Elba's portrayal of Bloodsport is anything like&nbsp;
the source material, his biggest weakness is bound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:09.280
to be his mental illness, including guilt that&nbsp;
sits on his shoulders like a thousand-ton weight.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:14.640
Bloodsport enters the world of comics in a bloody&nbsp;
rampage across Metropolis. Early in the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:19.760
you get the impression he's a disgruntled veteran&nbsp;
of the Vietnam War. He guns down random civilians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:22.720
all the while proclaiming that&nbsp;
they're wasting the freedoms he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:27.600
and others fought for. Eventually, we learn&nbsp;
Bloodsport didn't fight for anyone's freedoms.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:31.520
It's Superman's pal and Daily&nbsp;
Planet photojournalist Jimmy Olsen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:37.520
who discovers that Robert DuBois never served in&nbsp;
the military. Instead, he fled to Canada and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:42.720
younger brother Mickey took his place. Mickey&nbsp;
lost both of his arms and legs in the conflict,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:47.680
and it's Robert DuBois' guilt over his&nbsp;
brother's injuries that drive him to madness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:53.360
Superman #4 ends with Olsen finding Mickey and&nbsp;
bringing him to the still-rampaging Bloodsport,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:56.640
who collapses in tears at the&nbsp;
sight of his younger brother.

00:11:56.640 --> 00:12:00.160
If Elba's Bloodsport carries&nbsp;
a similarly guilty conscience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:04.560
being reminded of his mistakes could do&nbsp;
more damage to him than a Kryptonian's fist.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:08.800
Comedian Pete Davidson plays&nbsp;
Blackguard in The Suicide Squad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:12.880
and his biggest weakness is, well...&nbsp;
he doesn't really have any strengths.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:15.004
"I'm afraid to say you have died."

00:12:15.004 --> 00:12:15.900
"Okay."

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:20.880
Okay, so maybe that's not completely true.&nbsp;
Blackguard's real name is Richard Hertz and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:26.640
he was a common criminal before being recruited&nbsp;
by the powerful Metropolis organization the 1000.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:30.640
He wears armor capable of generating&nbsp;
an energy mace and energy shield;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:35.440
beyond that, he doesn't have a whole lot to&nbsp;
offer. He isn't particularly bright and while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:39.280
his armor would make him a huge threat&nbsp;
to just about anyone in the real world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:42.720
in the world of superheroes and&nbsp;
villains, it doesn't mean a whole lot.

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:46.800
Predictably, Blackguard doesn't survive&nbsp;
his stay with the Suicide Squad. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:52.160
the super strong General Wade Eiling turns&nbsp;
on his teammates in 2008's Suicide Squad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:57.040
#7, Blackguard is his first victim — and it&nbsp;
doesn't take much of an effort to kill him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.040 --> 00:13:01.520
Eiling grabs Blackguard and rips his head off&nbsp;
before the latter even knows what's happening.

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:08.560
Digger Harkness, a.k.a. Captain Boomerang,&nbsp;
first showed up in 1960's The Flash #117,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:12.720
kicking off a long career of being a&nbsp;
pain in the Scarlet Speedster's neck.

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:15.920
Along with being played by Jai&nbsp;
Courtney on the big screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:20.000
Captain Boomerang has been a mainstay&nbsp;
in the Suicide Squad comics for years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:25.040
While portrayals change as writers and artists&nbsp;
come and go, a regular hallmark of Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:31.360
Boomerang is also his biggest weakness as far as&nbsp;
Task Force X is concerned — he's arguably the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:36.000
consistently treacherous member of the Suicide&nbsp;
Squad, and it never seems to end well for him.

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:37.720
"You're free to go."

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:51.600
Hating Amanda Waller more than just about anyone&nbsp;
— a tall order in Task Force X — there isn't much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:57.120
Captain Boomerang won't do to escape his service,&nbsp;
to pull one over on Waller, or just to annoy her.

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:00.880
He's let teammates die when he could have&nbsp;
easily saved them, he's tricked teammates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:05.280
into killing themselves, and in the case of the&nbsp;
young Hack, he flat-out murdered a colleague.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:09.280
He's also disguised himself as other&nbsp;
supervillains to continue making money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:13.520
while working for the Suicide Squad, and&nbsp;
has pulled elaborate pranks on the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:17.360
team. His efforts have resulted in —&nbsp;
among other things — the thief having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:21.920
what little privileges he enjoyed revoked&nbsp;
by Amanda Waller, and in at least one case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:26.480
had him unceremoniously dropped from a&nbsp;
helicopter and stranded on a deserted island.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:30.320
Rick Flag's biggest weakness&nbsp;
is that the Suicide Squad is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:32.560
the last place he should be for his sanity.

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:36.240
On one hand there are the villains&nbsp;
and vigilantes recruited to the Squad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:40.560
on the other there's the Machiavellian&nbsp;
Amanda Waller, and between them is Joel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:45.040
Kinnaman's Rick Flag — a soldier who wants&nbsp;
nothing more than to serve his country.

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:49.520
His place in the hierarchy, the things he's&nbsp;
forced to do as a member of the Suicide Squad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:55.160
and his values as a soldier all combine to make&nbsp;
Flag the unluckiest person in Task Force X.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:59.440
"Theyre psychotic, antisocial&nbsp;
freaks. It makes no sense."

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:03.280
Flag would rather not be tied to career&nbsp;
criminals for his military service.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:07.520
During his time in both the comics and&nbsp;
the movies, Flag has worked with killers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:12.400
thieves, and worse. He's literally commanded&nbsp;
cannibals as part of his duties. It forces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:17.440
him to not only overlook pasts that many would&nbsp;
say shouldn't be overlooked, but often to turn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:22.160
a blind eye to the ugly crimes the recruits&nbsp;
commit in the present for Flag and the Squad.

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:26.640
But for better or worse, they are his&nbsp;
recruits, and as a soldier Flag can't help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:31.040
but feel responsible for them. Not to mention&nbsp;
that Amanda Waller doesn't share his feelings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:35.840
of responsibility, and will readily sacrifice&nbsp;
any member of the Squad without losing a wink&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:40.480
of sleep over it, and when the smoke clears,&nbsp;
he'll have to continue taking orders from her.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:45.600
Mayling Ng's Mongal is the daughter&nbsp;
of Mongul, an interstellar warlord&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:49.920
who's fought the likes of Superman to a&nbsp;
standstill. Depending on who you talk to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:54.000
Mongal's greatest weakness is either&nbsp;
her lust for battle or her family.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:58.320
Like her father and brother, Mongal is blessed&nbsp;
with superhuman strength and resilience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:03.040
Also like the rest of her family, Mongal revels&nbsp;
in battle, and that could prove her undoing in The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:08.160
Suicide Squad. If Ng's version of the character&nbsp;
is anywhere near as powerful as the one from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:12.400
source material, she'll be more than happy to&nbsp;
charge into any battlefield without thinking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:17.040
twice, and if the Squad comes up against tough&nbsp;
enough adversaries, that could get her killed.

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:20.720
If it should happen that Mongal's family&nbsp;
somehow makes an appearance in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:25.440
that could prove the key to her destruction.&nbsp;
Her brother, Mongul the Younger, kills Mongal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:30.960
in 2006's Green Lantern #8. Seeing a picture&nbsp;
of his father together with daughter and son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:35.360
Mongul the Younger proclaims that family&nbsp;
is a weakness. Unwilling to tolerate it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:39.200
Mongul decapitates his sister with a&nbsp;
single punch before she can respond.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:44.320
Nathan Fillion will be playing a&nbsp;
character named TDK in The Suicide Squad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:50.400
though to diehard comics fans TDK is better&nbsp;
known by the hilarious name Arm-Fall-Off-Boy.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:56.560
The character premieres in 1989's Secret Origins&nbsp;
#46 when he tries and fails to join the Legion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.560 --> 00:17:01.440
of Super-Heroes. TDK boasts the ability&nbsp;
to detach his arms and legs from his body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:04.960
and use them as blunt instruments. You&nbsp;
may have often heard people in movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:09.040
and TV shows threaten to tear someone's&nbsp;
arm off and beat them with it — well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:13.360
TDK is somewhat kinder. He tears his&nbsp;
own arm off and beats you with it.

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:19.120
TDK's biggest weakness is pretty glaring. His&nbsp;
power, while hilarious, is pretty ridiculous.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:23.680
If all he's doing is trying to surprise a friend&nbsp;
or get his buddies sick during a dinner party,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:27.920
sure, he's golden. But in an actual&nbsp;
battle, he's kind of limited.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:33.120
As soon as he tears off one arm, well, that's&nbsp;
it. He can only tear off the one arm because he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:37.920
doesn't have anything to tear the second arm off&nbsp;
with, and nothing to swing it with regardless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:41.520
That leaves his legs, without which&nbsp;
he'll have difficulty standing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:45.520
walking, running, or even crawling.&nbsp;
So if he does remove one of his legs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:48.800
he better be aiming for his&nbsp;
opponent's shins, or what's the point?

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:53.600
Daniela Melchior is set to play&nbsp;
Ratcatcher 2 in The Suicide Squad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:56.960
We don't know much about how she differs&nbsp;
from the Otis Flannegan version of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:56.960 --> 00:18:00.720
character beyond her gender, though&nbsp;
it seems likely — considering she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:04.800
actually referred to as Ratcatcher 2 in&nbsp;
the film's sneak preview trailer — that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:09.280
the Flannegan version is meant to have existed&nbsp;
at some point before the events of the film.

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:14.320
If Ratcatcher 2 is anything like her predecessor,&nbsp;
then it's likely her biggest vulnerability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:19.440
isn't tough to figure out. Flannegan is one of the&nbsp;
many villains to make Batman's life difficult in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:24.880
Gotham City, and as Ratcatcher he's learned to&nbsp;
train and command whole armies of rats. In spite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:29.360
of a pretty bizarre gimmick, his hordes of vermin&nbsp;
and his intimate knowledge of Gotham's sewer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:35.760
system make Flannegan a formidable foe for Batman&nbsp;
or any other vigilante trying to spoil his plans.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:40.880
But as far as we can tell, The Suicide Squad&nbsp;
isn't set in Gotham City. Which leaves Ratcatcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:45.760
2 possibly dependent on two things — an army of&nbsp;
rats and a knowledge of Gotham's sewers — that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:50.320
will be of minimum help to her. Obviously, she's&nbsp;
going to be in the film for a reason, though it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:54.480
tough to imagine exactly how she's going to&nbsp;
transport armies of rats all over the place.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:19:00.160
David Dastmalchian will play the Polka-Dot Man&nbsp;
in The Suicide Squad. Along with Condiment King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:04.480
and Kite Man, Polka-Dot Man is one of those&nbsp;
corny Batman villains who doesn't really fit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:08.880
in the kind of gritty, dark Batman stories&nbsp;
the general public is used to these days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:14.160
and usually only surfaces as part of a gag or a&nbsp;
parody like LEGO Batman. But now the bad guy who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:19.040
looks like a Twister board is graduating to the&nbsp;
live-action big leagues with the Suicide Squad.

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:22.320
Without knowing how this version&nbsp;
of Polka-Dot Man will be portrayed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:26.320
just judging by the fact that he's&nbsp;
named Polka-Dot Man makes us suspect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.320 --> 00:19:30.640
his biggest weakness will be the challenge&nbsp;
of being taken seriously by his comrades.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:35.600
Polka-Dot Man is pretty low on the pecking order&nbsp;
of Gotham City's long list of bad guys, and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:40.400
knows it better than anyone else. It's likely&nbsp;
he's going to feel like he has a lot to prove.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:44.400
On the other hand, it's easy to imagine&nbsp;
Polka-Dot Man's biggest weakness could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:47.920
also be one of his greatest strengths.&nbsp;
Think about it — if you were attacked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:52.400
by a villain calling himself Polka-Dot Man,&nbsp;
how long would it take you to stop laughing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:56.320
and how much damage could he do to you while&nbsp;
you were busy not taking him seriously?

00:19:57.040 --> 00:20:02.240
Surprising no one, Margot Robbie will reprise&nbsp;
her role as Harley Quinn in The Suicide Squad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:05.840
Thanks to the events of 2020's Birds&nbsp;
of Prey, the weakness that would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:09.200
been assigned to her a few years&nbsp;
ago isn't in the picture anymore.

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:23.280
Most fans would likely agree that it wasn't&nbsp;
that long ago that Harley's biggest weakness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:28.400
had one name — Joker. In both the animated&nbsp;
series that first brought Harley to life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:33.520
and in the comics that followed, Harley couldn't&nbsp;
resist the Joker. No matter how many times he hurt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:38.160
her, no matter how many times he betrayed her,&nbsp;
Harley would always welcome her "puddin'" back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:43.200
with open arms. But after the events of Birds&nbsp;
of Prey, Harley's learned to be independent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:46.960
and we don't think she'd even be tempted&nbsp;
to take Joker back if he returned.

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:53.040
No, instead Harley's biggest vulnerability is also&nbsp;
perhaps her greatest strength, and arguably the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:58.800
main reason she's of any use to the Suicide Squad.&nbsp;
Harley has no fear. In spite of having no special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:03.440
metahuman abilities to call her own, Harley would&nbsp;
wade into a hail of bullets if she thought it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:07.920
a fun thing to do, and she'd do it laughing.&nbsp;
It's part of what makes her so dangerous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:12.000
though it could ultimately send her to that&nbsp;
creepy, abandoned amusement park in the sky.

